-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Ruff and Reddy
  Publisher   Hi-Tec, 1990
  Version     1.0

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Ruff and Reddy in the Space Adventure (1990)(Hi-Tec)(128K).z80
  MD5         4b6c490438881cb23d0993d4b32788a2

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

  Memory      Any Next: a 1MB Next has the memory for the game. Enhanced needs
              a 1MB Next, and is not offered on a smaller one.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures are drawn on the Next's own graphics layers, so they keep their
  own colours and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is
  unchanged.

  Colours     Default (the game's own) plus: Enhanced, chosen on the menu, off
              by default.
  Enhanced    Ynicky's Spec256 colours as the set paints them: red, cyan and
              blue rock with a black sea, brown Ruff, painted Lilli-Punies and
              items, and the coloured panel. Nothing repainted. Source:
              Enhanced colours: Ynicky (Spec256).

  Pace        original (+0.12% measured in JNext 1.1.104, against the original
              on a 128K machine, at the player's update, input applied after
              the game's read, game state in lockstep)

  Changes     1.0: figures in their own white on a double-buffered Layer 2, in
              the game's own plot order, over the original bitmap; scenery in
              its own attributes; Enhanced colours from the Spec256 set on a
              full Layer 2, a menu option, off by default; the render pass and
              the copy run whole at 28 MHz in pace windows; a loading screen
              from the same game's tape; Sinclair's 48K ROM as the whole alt
              ROM (NextZXOS 26.11 safe); four cheats from the archive, tested

  Note        Keys: on the game's menu 1 keyboard (Q up, A down, O left, P
              right, SPACE fire), 2 Kempston, 3 Interface 2. In play key 1
              pauses, fire resumes, Q in the pause gives up. Default: the
              original look with the clash gone: a figure keeps its white on
              coloured rock. Enhanced, on the menu, off by default: the
              Spec256 colours on Layer 2 over the unchanged game, black sea
              included. The 128K release, with its AY music. Fits a 1MB Next.
              Known issues: pace in JNext: default +0.00% to +0.12% over whole
              runs, slowest 20-update stretch +1.59%; Enhanced -0.14% to
              -0.00% over whole runs, quiet thirds -0.02% to +0.01%, busy
              thirds -0.39% to +0.02%, 12 runs in 4 scenes; Enhanced slowest
              20-update stretch +0.04%. In Enhanced the panel's digits and
              item boxes keep the original colours. Missing: natural play to
              the end (most of the map by a test poke only); Interface 2 not
              tried; hardware untested.

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  Infinite lives
   2  Infinite time
   3  Immunity
   4  Card, fuel pump and TNT

  Cheats come from the archive's POKEs for this release.

