-- TESTING -------------------------------------------------------------------
  Tested      Run by script through the real loader on a NextZXOS 26.11 card
              copy, default and Enhanced; 1.0 not yet played by the owner;
              published at his request

  Replay      Enhanced: 9 recordings, 61231 frames, the first room, rooms 13,
              16, 22, 34 and level complete by test copies: 30875 hooks run
              original and build from one state each: every register including
              R and all 48K RAM: IDENTICAL; 5033 Layer 2 pictures, 206151680
              pixels, against a picture built from the room map and the plots,
              and the game's own buffer against the same model in mono:
              IDENTICAL; 9 of 9 broken builds caught; 512 ABI cases; the
              start-up exact with and without NEXLOAD. Default: the same
              recordings and 9 of 9 broken builds, 640 ABI cases, boot exact

  Emulator    JNext 1.1.104 headless: through the real .NEXCLASH loader on a
              private NextZXOS 26.11 card copy, default, default with cheats,
              Enhanced and Enhanced with cheats, output byte for byte as
              nxc.py makes it, reaching play; 15-minute soak of Enhanced
              against the original with the sheet viewed; flicker check clean;
              the flip outside the play rows

  Coverage    Scripted input, no human play: the first rooms, menus, deaths,
              game over and a new game; giving up in the pause; rooms 13, 16,
              22, 34 and level complete by test copies; not reached: most of
              the map, natural level completion, the end of the game,
              Interface 2

  Hardware    none

  Nothing here claims a result on real hardware unless the line above says so.

-- HOW TO USE ----------------------------------------------------------------
  Put this .nxc and the game file in the same folder on the Next's card and
  choose the .nxc in the Browser. See README.txt.
